<%# BMI hero result — regenerated from spec issue #53 against DESIGN.md (BLEND, §4).

    A richer-than-a-single-number answer:
      • Hero-result (DESIGN.md §4): the big tabular-nums BMI on a surface card with the
        5px coral left rule, kg/m² unit, and the WHO category as a green accent badge
        (positive-stat green, DESIGN.md §1 — text carries the meaning, colour reinforces,
        never colour alone per §6).
      • WHO scale + marker (DESIGN.md §4 / spec): a thin stacked bar plotting the four
        broad WHO bins across a 15–40 window, the band containing this person lifted to
        accent green, with an ink marker tick pinning the exact BMI.
      • Responsive auto-fit stat grid (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid"): the WHO bands rendered
        as a `.stat-grid` of `.stat-card`s — label + range, the active band in ink with an
        accent dot, the rest faint — so the classification reads as text (DESIGN.md §6)
        and the cards wrap/flow without clipping at any panel width.

    `calc:` is a valid Calculators::Bmi; the rendered result keys are `bmi` + `category`
    (the JSON envelope's result shape, ARCHITECTURE.md §4). %>
<% bmi = calc.result[:bmi] %>
<% category = calc.result[:category] %>
<% bands = bmi_scale_bands(bmi) %>
<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
  <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
    <%# The 5px coral left rule (DESIGN.md §4 Hero-result). %>
    <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Body Mass Index</p>
      <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
        <p class="text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink"><%= bmi_display(bmi) %></p>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-faint">kg/m&sup2;</p>
      </div>

      <%# Category badge — the WHO band as a green accent chip. The text is the meaning;
          colour is reinforcement, not the sole signal (DESIGN.md §6). %>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-bold text-accent">
          <%= category %>
        </span>
      </p>

      <%# WHO classification scale — a thin stacked bar over the 15–40 window. Each broad
          bin sizes to its share of the window; the active bin (the one containing this
          BMI) lifts to accent green, and a marker tick pins the exact BMI. The bar is
          decorative — the stat grid below names the bands as text. %>
      <div class="mt-6 relative">
        <div class="flex h-2.5 overflow-hidden rounded-full" role="presentation">
          <% bands.each do |band| %>
            <span class="block h-full <%= band[:active] ? "bg-accent" : "bg-rule" %>"
                  style="width: <%= band[:width] %>%" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <%# Marker — a thin ink tick at this BMI's position along the bar. It lives in the
            relative wrapper (not the overflow-hidden bar) so it is never clipped. %>
        <span class="absolute -top-1 h-4.5 w-0.5 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-ink"
              style="left: <%= bmi_marker_position(bmi) %>%" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      <%# Band legend — a responsive auto-fit stat grid (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid"): each
          band is a stat card (label + range), the active band in ink with an accent dot,
          the rest faint. Carries the classification as text (DESIGN.md §6) and wraps/flows
          without clipping at any width. %>
      <dl class="mt-6 stat-grid">
        <% bands.each do |band| %>
          <div class="stat-card <%= band[:active] ? "text-ink" : "text-faint" %>">
            <dt class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-bold">
              <% if band[:active] %><span class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span><% end %>
              <%= band[:label] %>
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 text-lg font-bold tracking-[-0.01em] tabular-nums"><%= band[:range] %></dd>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
